## EXACT NUMBERS — TIER 1 (Never Compress, Never Approximate)

### From 1.1 — Phase Prerequisites
| Phase | Revenue | Prerequisite to Enter |
|-------|---------|----------------------|
| 1 | $0→$40K/mo | None. Find product-market fit. |
| 2 | $40K→$100K/mo | Have an offer that converts cold strangers into high-ticket clients ($3K/mo+ agency, $4K+ coaching) |
| 3 | $100K→$250K/mo | Have consistent, repeatable sales process (30%+ close) AND fulfillment conveyor belt |
| 4 | $250K→$500K/mo | Both sales and fulfillment running at/above KPI without founder on frontlines |
| 5 | $500K→$1M/mo | Department managers installed (promoted from within, never external hires) |

### From 1.3 — Starting Prices (New Offers)
| Type | Price | Terms |
|------|-------|-------|
| Agency | $2.5K-$3K/mo | 3-4 month minimum |
| Coaching (biz opp) | $4,800 | 12-16 weeks |
| Coaching (health/relationships) | $2,800-$3,800 | 12-16 weeks |

### From 1.3 — Existing Offer Prices
| Type | Price | Terms |
|------|-------|-------|
| Agency | $3K/mo+ | 4 months minimum |
| Coaching (biz opp) | $6,800+ | 12-16 weeks |
| Coaching (health/relationships) | $4,800+ | 12-16 weeks |

### From 1.3 — Price Increase Triggers
- Close rate ABOVE 30% AND cash collected ABOVE 50% → increase price by $2K on the package
- Stair-step until diminishing returns between price + close rate
- Re-offer everyone who didn't close at the higher price

### From 1.4 — KPI Benchmarks (Exact)
| Metric | KPI Target | Notes |
|--------|-----------|-------|
| Ad Spend Ratio | 2:1 new cash:ad spend | Below 2:1 = find constraint |
| CPBC (Cost Per Booked Call) | < $300 | B2C could be $100-$200 |
| SUR % (Show-Up Rate) | B2C: 50%+ / B2B: 65%+ | = calls taken / (calls booked - cancelled by you) |
| Close Rate | 25%+ | 20%→30% = 50% front-end revenue increase |
| Cash Collected % | 40%+ | |
| Cash ROAS | 2x minimum | Day 1 target |
| Revenue ROAS | 5x minimum | |
| Churn | < 10% | = clients leaving / total active clients entering month. New clients NOT counted. |
| NOI | 45%+ (target 50-55%) | |

### From 1.6 — P&L Allocation Targets (Exact)
| Category | Target % of Revenue |
|----------|-------------------|
| Marketing/Acquisition | 20% (spend MORE if below this) |
| Total Labor | 20-25% |
| — Fulfillment labor | 9% |
| — Sales labor | 8% |
| — Operations/Marketing staff | 3% |
| — Finance/Legal/HR | 5% (overflow until big enough) |
| Overhead | 5% |
| **NOI** | **50-55%** |

### From 1.6 — Variable vs Fixed Cost Rule
- Variable costs ONLY until $150K-$200K/mo revenue
- AMs = $ per client (variable)
- Closers/setters = commission only (variable)
- CSMs = $ per client (variable)
- Fixed costs introduced only after $150K-$200K/mo

### From 1.6 — Compensation Examples (Exact)
**AM Example:** OTE = $10K/mo. Target = 7% of P&L. At $4K/mo price → 35 clients under management @ $285/client. At $5.5K/mo price → 25 clients @ $400/client = 7.2% of P&L.

**Closer Example:** OTE = $15K/mo. Target = 5% of P&L. At $5K/mo price ($20K package/4mo) → 10% commission. 100 calls/mo @ 25% close = 25 clients. $500K revenue, 50% upfront cash = $250K collected. Commission = $25K. Need $125K in AR to hit 5% of P&L.

### From 1.8 — LTGP:CAC Formulas (Exact)
```
Retention rate (months) = 100 / (100 × churn rate)
LTV = retention rate × monthly price
Lifetime COGs = monthly COGs × retention rate
LTGP = LTV - Lifetime COGs
CAC = total ad spend / total clients closed (same period)
LTGP:CAC = LTGP / CAC
```

### From 1.8 — The 6 Levers (Exact)
**Decrease CAC:**
1. Cheaper CPQBC (cost per qualified booked call)
2. Higher show rate
3. Higher close rate

**Increase LTGP:**
4. Charge more (increase prices)
5. Decrease costs to fulfill (lower COGs)
6. Keep clients paying longer (reduce churn)

**Nothing else affects profitability outside these 6.**

### From 1.8 — Broken Model Test
If you CANNOT decrease COGs AND CANNOT increase price → model is fundamentally broken. Needs restructuring (different service, different deliverable, different market positioning).

### From 4.2 — AM Model Numbers
| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| AM OTE | $10K-$15K/mo |
| CSD direct report capacity | 7 AMs |
| Total client capacity (CSD structure) | 140-245 clients |
| Founder acts as CSD until | ~$250K/mo |

### From 4.3 — Onboarding Timeline
| Milestone | Timeframe |
|-----------|-----------|
| OB experience completion target | First 5-7 days |
| OB call scheduling | Within 1-3 days of onboarding |
| OB call duration | 60 minutes |

### From 4.7 — AM Schedule Metrics
